results/*
!results/.gitkeep
# Keystone reproducibility artifact (paper Table 2 / sec:measure); tracked on purpose.
!results/b_insuff
results/b_insuff/*
!results/b_insuff/matched_pairs.csv
!results/b_insuff/decomposition.json
# Named as its source by App. C (the input-fixed kernel control) and by the binning
# enumeration the main text quotes; tracked so a reader can open what the paper cites.
!results/b_insuff/fidelity_lever_inputfixed.json
!results/b_insuff/binning_conventions.json
# The admissibility of every stratum in the map -- which cells may be stated as a finding and
# which are reported only -- and the overlap between strata that decides what may not be
# counted twice.  Regenerated by the same script as the map, so a claim and its admissibility
# travel together; tracked because the map's verdicts are unreadable without them.
!results/b_insuff/admissibility_table.csv
!results/b_insuff/admissibility.json
!results/b_insuff/stratum_overlap.csv
# The converged 90% interval on the one stratified finding, and the Monte-Carlo error the map's
# own 3000-draw bootstrap carries.  The abstract quotes this interval, and until 2026-08-07 the
# submission printed four independent 3000-draw replicates of it as four different numbers, so
# the converged value is versioned and make_map_table_tex.py reads it at build time.
!results/b_insuff/glycol_ether_ci_converged.json
# The same question asked of every interval the map prints, 2026-08-10: one printing precision
# per row set, chosen from that row set's own Monte-Carlo error and verified on the run that
# bought it.  make_map_table_tex.py reads it at build time -- the map tables cannot be generated
# without it -- and its `as_submitted' block is the record of what each stratum NAME printed while
# the bootstrap was still seeded from the name, which the repair makes identical and would
# otherwise erase.  The snapshot that block is computed from is versioned beside it; the two
# replicate CSVs behind them (4800 + 960 rows) are regenerable from the deposited seed sequences
# and are not, exactly as the glycol replicates above are not.
!results/b_insuff/map_ci_precision.json
!results/b_insuff/map_ci_precision_table.csv
!results/b_insuff/stratified_map_table_pre_rowset_seed.csv
# The constant-offset control that qualifies the transfer ratio of Sec. 6.4 / App. E.
# Small, and it is the only source for a number the paper prints, so it is versioned.
!results/compensation
results/compensation/*
!results/compensation/offset_control.json
# The external closure anchor: the deployed COSMO-SAC-2002 scored on the PGL6ed
# infinite-dilution set that de Souza et al. (IECR 2025) evaluate COSMO-SAC on.
# The three upstream record files are versioned with it (328 kB) because the
# comparison is only checkable if the row set travels with the number; the
# component map is deposited as the used subset, not the 2.8 MB original, and the
# script reads whichever is present.  scored_records.csv is the per-row evidence
# behind the anchor table and is what a referee re-derives the AAD from.
!results/published_idac_check
results/published_idac_check/*
!results/published_idac_check/summary.json
!results/published_idac_check/summary.csv
!results/published_idac_check/table_closure_anchor.tex
!results/published_idac_check/component_map_used.csv
!results/published_idac_check/scored_records.csv
!results/published_idac_check/pgl6ed_source
# The external-baseline table (this work vs FastSolv/SolProp, re-run and as published)
# and the locked per-row predictions the ln x2 parity figure is drawn from.
!results/external_baseline_comparison
results/external_baseline_comparison/*
!results/external_baseline_comparison/summary.json
!results/external_baseline_comparison/table_rows.csv
!results/external_baseline_comparison/table_article.tex
!results/external_baseline_comparison/parity_rows_seed42.csv
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep

