# line says it may safely be deleted.
paper/acs-*.bib

# Per-arm metrics behind Figure 2 and its rows of Table 2. The per-row prediction files are ~5 MB
# each and go to the archive; these summaries are what a reader needs to recompute every number the
# figure prints, so they are versioned.
!results/e5_sigma_grounding
results/e5_sigma_grounding/*
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_42
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_43
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_44
results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_4?/*
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_4?/comparison.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/seed_4?/*.summary.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/THREE_SEED_SUMMARY.md
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ROW_SET_DECOMPOSITION.md
# The two Section S1 slices of the substitution, each regenerable in seconds by the script named in
# its own header: scripts/analysis/run_paradox_channel_split.py (the -0.000/+0.431/+0.006 row-class
# split) and scripts/analysis/run_substitution_perturbation.py (the T_m / dH_fus / Phi maxima).
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/section_s1_channel_split.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/section_s1_substitution_perturbation.json

# Gate A1, the leak-free re-run.  Same shape as the published run above: the per-seed cross-arm
# comparison and the per-arm summaries, never the multi-megabyte prediction CSVs.  Note the file
# name: comparison_both_arms.json, not comparison.json -- each arm ran as its own process and the
# later one overwrote comparison.json with a single arm, so that file is NOT a cross-arm comparison
# and is deliberately left untracked.
!results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree
results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/*
!results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/seed_4?
results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/seed_4?/*
!results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/seed_4?/comparison_both_arms.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/seed_4?/*.summary.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding_leakfree/GATE_A1_RECORD.md
# The solvent-ranking working behind Table S17 and the ranking paragraphs of Sec. 3.1 / S6:
# the three-seed ranking and floor analysis, the paired arm-minus-own-floor intervals, and the
# in-sample/leave-one-out affine recalibration with the per-group fitted slopes. The scripts read
# the ~5 MB per-row prediction files (archive) and write these JSONs, which carry every number the
# two documents print, so they are versioned and the per-group CSVs are not.
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking
results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/*
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final.py
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final_floorci.py
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final_floorci.json
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final_oos.py
!results/e5_sigma_grounding/ranking/rank_final_oos.json

# Deposits behind numbers the manuscript prints, un-ignored for the same reason the
# b_insuff ones are: a printed figure whose artifact is not in the tree is a figure a
# reader cannot check, and three of them were hand-transcribed from scratch files before
# these existed.
!results/profile_db_vs_iteration
results/profile_db_vs_iteration/*
!results/profile_db_vs_iteration/cross.json
!results/multifragment_stratum
results/multifragment_stratum/*
!results/multifragment_stratum/summary.json
!results/solver_iteration_audit
